<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Dreux</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Dreux was a cadet branch of the French royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capetian-dynasty">Capetian dynasty</a>, descended from Robert I, Count of Dreux, a son of Louis VI. In 1213 Philip II married the Breton heiress Alix to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-i-duke-of-brittany">Peter Mauclerc</a> of Dreux, whose descendants, including the later Montfort dukes, ruled the Duchy of Brittany until the line ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany">Anne of Brittany</a> in 1514.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-dreux.jpg" alt="House of Dreux" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlodangio · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Robert_de_Dreux.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
